BASELINE split (C=4 both, SIS): chi2=119.9 (dof=15) -> 8.8 sigma
  (Brouwer report >=6 sigma; validates point-by-point against the released profiles)
  early-type g_obs ABOVE late in 15/15 bins; mean dlog10(g_obs)=0.261 dex
  -> early types sit ABOVE (excess g_obs / baryon-deficient) late on the RAR

=== AXIS 1: ESD->g_obs conversion differential (C in [pi,4.76], type-differential) ===
  C_early  C_late  dlogC(dex)  split_sigma   note
   4.00    4.00   +0.000       8.8      uniform C=4 (=baseline, no differential)
   3.53    4.33   -0.089       5.0      physical: early c-high (x~10) vs late (x~1)
   3.43    4.76   -0.142       3.0      aggressive concentration differential
   3.14    4.76   -0.180       1.9      EXTREME: early point-mass vs late inner-NFW (implausible)
  -> a PHYSICAL concentration differential erodes but does NOT kill the split; only an implausibly
     extreme (point-mass-early) C-differential removes it. Conversion is a real but partial systematic.

