  median required differential M_gas/M* = 1.09  (authors' estimate: M_gas~M* = 1.0; their arithmetic: 0.15dex->1.0, 0.20dex->1.5)
  mean vertical split = 0.261 dex  (deep-MOND slope ~0.5 -> ~2x horizontal)
  -> compare to post-2023 eROSITA CGM stacks (next): is a DIFFERENTIAL M_gas/M* of this size plausible
     for ISOLATED M*<1e11 early-vs-late, given late types ALSO carry CGM?

=== AXIS 2 verdict — eROSITA CGM constraint (Zhang+2025, eRASS Paper III; POST-dates Brouwer) ===
  Brouwer sample is M* < 1e11 (log M* < 11.0). eROSITA Paper III stacks quiescent (early) vs
  star-forming (late) galaxies and finds, VERBATIM, 'no significant differences in their hot CGM
  X-ray emission' BELOW log M* = 11.0. A differential appears only at log M* > 11.0 (~3x in L_X),
  and even there it is HALO-MASS driven (equal CGM at fixed halo mass), NOT an intrinsic early-type
  CGM excess. => the differential M_gas/M* ~ 1.1 the gas escape REQUIRES is ~an order of magnitude
  above what eROSITA permits in the relevant regime. The authors' 2021 hedge ('corrections likely
  moderate') is now quantifiable with data they did not have: the gas escape is DISFAVOURED.
  Caveat (both-ways): eROSITA traces the HOT (~1e6-7 K) phase only; a cool/warm differential is not
  directly excluded, but is not independently motivated and would itself need to be ~M_gas=M* differential.

======================================================================
COMBINED VERDICT (pre-registered outcomes; hostility INVERTED):
  baseline split           : 8.8 sigma (validates Brouwer >=6 sigma point-by-point)
  - physical conversion diff: erodes to 5.0 sigma (real ~0.09 dex systematic; survives)
  - gas escape (M_gas~M*)   : DISFAVOURED by eROSITA (no hot-CGM differential below 1e11)
  => OUTCOME A (with a residual-C caveat on conversion): the split HARDENS the exposure AGAINST
     property-independent modified gravity. Locked wording: NOT 'LCDM confirmed' -- MICE and BAHAMAS
     disagree with each other about the split in simulations, so this is an exposure to the FRAMEWORK,
     not a confirmation of a specific dark-matter model. Reported at full weight per the #1 rule.
